Script-tag balance was off (15 open vs 17 close). Two whole blocks had
no opening <script> tag at all, so the browser rendered their raw
source — CSS, HTML template strings, function bodies — as literal
text on the page instead of executing it:

1. The entire inlined 'TSM Mission Guide' widget (~293 lines: styles,
   render(), renderMission(), bindEvents(), regenerateSteps(), init())
   sat directly in the body between the previous </script> and its own
   trailing </script>, unwrapped.
2. The 'TSM AUTO-RUN STRATEGIST' IIFE right after it had the same
   problem — no opening tag, closed by a stray </script> with nothing
   to pair with.

This is the same systemic 'script tag leak' pattern flagged before
(automated patch injector omitting opening <script> tags) — this
instance just hadn't been hit yet because nothing had broken loudly
until the visible-text render made it obvious.

Fix: inserted the two missing opening <script> tags so both blocks
close against the </script> tags that were already there. Verified
<script>/</script> count is now balanced (17/17) and every non-src
script block in the file still passes node --check individually.

Noted but not fixed here (separate, non-urgent issue): the page also
loads /html/tsm-insurance/public/js/tsm-mission-guide.js, which does
not exist anywhere in the repo — a dead 404'ing include, harmless
since nothing depends on it, but worth cleaning up in the same pass
as other dead-script sweeps.
